# Motoko mission profile (bootstrap 2026-08-12; iteration 0 pending).
# Sourced by tools/launchd/mission-control.sh when launchd sets MISSION_PROFILE=motoko.
# Convention: every optional entry uses ${VAR:-value} so a command-line env pin still wins.

MISSION_NAME=motoko
MISSION_REPO=sunholo-data/ailang
MISSION_DOC=design_docs/motoko-mission.md
# 2026-08-18: was a BARE assignment, violating this file's own ${VAR:-value}
# convention. pin-root.sh exports MISSION_WORKDIR=<pinned worktree> and re-execs;
# the driver sets REPO from it at line 40 (correct), but THIS file is re-sourced at
# line 47 and clobbered it back — so the "driver pin:" log line named the stale
# source clone while the loop actually ran the pinned worktree. Behaviour was right,
# the provenance line was the opposite of the truth. Now the pin wins.
MISSION_WORKDIR="${MISSION_WORKDIR:-/Users/voightkampff/dev/sunholo-data/ailang-motoko}"
# --- PATH (do NOT remove — this is the World mission's five-iteration bug) ------
# The shared driver only PREPENDS $HOME/go/bin:$HOME/.local/bin to $PATH. launchd's
# PATH is restricted and carries no /opt/homebrew/bin, so without this line `codex`,
# `gh`, `go` and `node` all resolve rc=127 — which the driver's codex pre-flight reads
# as a FAILED PROBE and silently demotes the ratified codex lane to opus on EVERY fire.
# World burned iterations 18/19/21/22 mis-attributing that to a spent quota and an
# unusable pin before iteration 23 confirmed it first-party (`grep -c PATH` on the
# World plist == 0). The driver is FROZEN CORE and this file is sourced after the
# driver's PATH line but BEFORE the probe, so this is the correct home for the fix.
PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:$PATH

# --- Routing --------------------------------------------------------------------
# No executor override. The driver already implements the ratified chain
# (codex:gpt-5.6-sol -> pi:openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731:floor -> opus,
# ailang#611), which is non-Anthropic-first — so this second concurrent loop does not
# double the Anthropic burn. Do NOT hard-pin a lane here: the V1 profile's history
# shows a pin that is not codex:* makes the driver's codex pre-flight branch never
# run, so nothing probes the lane and a refilled bucket goes unnoticed for days.
#
# To force a lane for a specific fire, pin on the command line instead:
#   MISSION_PROFILE=motoko MISSION_EXECUTOR_MODEL=opus tools/launchd/mission-control.sh
